meanings=[\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"other\",\"other\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"en dash\",\"baseline dot\",\"space\",\"comma\",\"nothing\",\"comma\",\"other\",\"space\",\"space\",\"space\",\"nothing\",\"baseline dot\",\"space\",\"baseline dot\",\"em dash\",\"nothing\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"space\",\"space\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"em dash\",\"baseline dot\",\"comma\",\"space\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"other\",\"baseline dot\",\"nothing\",\"other\",\"space\",\"space\",\"other\",\"en dash\",\"hyphen\",\"hyphen\",\"nothing\",\"en dash\",\"comma\",\"em dash\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"space\",\"baseline dot\",\"comma\",\"space\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"space\",\"space\",\"comma\",\"nothing\",\"baseline dot\",\"nothing\",\"space\",\"en dash\",\"nothing\",\"en dash\",\"nothing\",\"nothing\",\"baseline dot\",\"nothing\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"hyphen\",\"unreadable\",\"hyphen\",\"baseline dot\",\"other\",\"other\",\"baseline dot\",\"baseline dot\",\"nothing\",\"baseline dot\"]
low={31,50,61,78}
notes={31:'Stroke length near the two-digit threshold.',50:'Blurred stroke length near the two-digit threshold.',61:'Trailing gap is close to the crop edge.',78:'Whole rotated block; target gap cannot be located reliably.'}
with open('answers.jsonl','w') as f:
 for n,(x,y) in enumerate(zip(items,meanings),1):
  f.write(json.dumps(dict(item_id=x['item_id'],answer=next(k for k,v in x['options'].items() if v==y),confidence='low' if n in low else 'high',note=notes.get(n,'')))+'\\n')
a=[json.loads(s) for s in open('answers.jsonl')]
assert len(a)==len(items)==86
assert [s['item_id'] for s in a]==[s['item_id'] for s in items]
assert len({s['item_id'] for s in a})==86
assert all(s['answer'] in x['options'] for s,x in zip(a,items))
assert all(s['confidence'] in ('high','low') for s in a)
print('Validated count, order, unique items, option letters, and confidence values.')
print(dict(collections.Counter(x['options'][s['answer']] for x,s in zip(items,a))))
print('Low confidence:',sum(s['confidence']=='low' for s in a))
